index cea32e6..8c2d49f 100644
--- a/docs/pysemver.rst
+++ b/docs/pysemver.rst
@@ -137,6 +137,65 @@ to indicates which is the bigger version:
 * ``1`` if the first version is greater than the second version.
 
 
+pysemver sort
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Sort versions, oldest first.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver sort [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to sort. If none are given, versions are read from *standard in*,
+    one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The sorted versions are printed on *standard out* as plain text, one
+version per line, so the output can be read line by line in a shell script:
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+    $ pysemver sort 1.10.0 1.2.0 1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0-rc.1
+    1.2.0
+    1.10.0
+    $ printf '1.10.0\n1.2.0\n' | pysemver sort
+    1.2.0
+    1.10.0
+
+If any version is invalid, nothing is printed on standard out and the
+return code is ``2``.
+
+
+pysemver latest
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Print the highest version that is not a prerelease.
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+   pysemver latest [<VERSION>...]
+
+.. option:: <VERSION>
+
+    Versions to check. If none are given, versions are read from *standard in*,
+    one per line; blank lines are ignored.
+
+The result is printed on *standard out* as a JSON object. If all versions
+are prereleases (or there are none), the value is ``null``:
+
+.. code:: bash
+
+    $ pysemver latest 1.2.0 2.0.0-rc.1 1.10.0
+    {"latest": "1.10.0"}
+    $ pysemver latest 1.0.0-rc.1
+    {"latest": null}
+
+If any version is invalid, nothing is printed on standard out and the
+return code is ``2``.
+
+
 Return Code
 -----------
 
